    "name": "target-per-period-the-period-that-begins-in-the-published-month",
    "why": "The seam case, asserting an EMPTY expectation on purpose. This block began on 26 July, in a month somebody else already published: p-ali took two duties there and two in the draft, which is exactly the target of four. Dropping the carry-in tail from the count turns that clean row into a shortfall of two, so the empty list is the assertion. The seam guard's other half then takes the history away and requires the same call to go quiet: a period whose first six days were never supplied is unknown rather than empty, and a target may not treat unknown as zero — it would report a shortfall against a block nobody can see.",
